# Shared learning

Durable project facts go in files both tools read — `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — not in `~/.cursor/` or `~/.claude/`.

Same claim in every copy. One concern per rule, under 50 lines. How you run git stays in your user rules.

A sentence in `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or a Cursor rule that the code makes false is deleted or rewritten in the same change.

This repository publishes `index.html` and nothing else. Do not add docs, source, or a second copy of the policy. Do not edit `index.html` here.

How a lesson climbs is `.cursor/rules/refinement-ladder.mdc`.
